{"title":"How to Say “YES” to Your Life","link":"https://www.themarginalian.org/2026/10/01/yes/","date":1790878946000,"content":"<p>It started with an <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2025/07/25/urns/\">urn for living</a> gone wrong, the clay kiltering off center, resisting my every effort to force it back into shape. The harder I pushed to control it, the more it took on a life of its own, folding like flesh, bending like mind. I pushed and despaired, pushed and despaired, until, exhausted and exasperated, I gave up and simply let my hands follow the momentum of the clay, saying “YES” to its will. </p>\n<p>And then, magic: I watched the vessel turn into what I could have never imagined, never created by force: an enormous seashell, a miniature Guggenheim, a great open ear — asymmetrical yet perfect in its secret logic, the proof beyond the postulate. </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/donate/\"><img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel01.jpg?resize=680%2C655&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"655\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel01.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel01.jpg?resize=320%2C308&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel01.jpg?resize=600%2C578&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel01.jpg?resize=240%2C231&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel01.jpg?resize=768%2C740&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p>Here was an antidote to all the urns and <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2025/10/23/ceramic-sentences/\">bowls</a> I had controlled into perfect symmetry, almost factory-like, pushing so hard to center that a stress injury incapacitated my left arm for seven months. Here was a hard, fragile material — pulverized stone that vitrifies like glass — taking a soft, organic shape.</p>\n<p>I found myself wondering what life itself would be like if, rather than willing it to conform to our design only to end up in despair, we simply said “YES” to its will, collaborating with rather than resisting the centrifugal force of the heart, the angular momentum of memory, the gravity of change. “YES” to <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2023/11/12/necessary-losses/\">the necessary losses</a>. “YES” to <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2022/11/24/david-bowie-creativity-advice/\">the fear that signals growth</a>. “YES” to the death of the dream of perfection.</p>\n<p>“The great difficulty is to say Yes to life,” James Baldwin observed in reckoning with <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2021/06/06/james-baldwin-giovannis-room-love-choice/\">the paradox of freedom</a> not long after Viktor Frankl looked back on surviving the Holocaust to insist that our task here is to say <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2020/05/17/yes-to-life-in-spite-of-everything-viktor-frankl/\">“yes to life in spite of everything.”</a></p>\n<p>Beyond basic physical survival, most of our psychological suffering, when closely examined, is a form of saying “NO” to life — a refusal, vehement or subtle, to bend the idea of how things should be to the raw reality of how they are, the reality that is the only arena in which we can act to change anything. All things not pliant enough to bend will break — fragility is a function of rigidity. </p>\n<p>We contact this elemental law most clearly and most painfully in relationships, which have a will of their own greater than the sum of two intents and which are never, however reciprocal, perfectly symmetrical. Have too rigid an idea of what a relationship should be, and it will inevitably shatter; look back on the most enduring and rewarding relationships of your life, and you will discover that they have found their own right form, different from your first intent, a form that is never final.</p>\n<p>And yet, paradoxically, <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2024/05/03/polyvagal-theory/\">rupture and repair</a> are how relationships are stress-tested and fortified across the long horizon of life. In this regard, love is more like embroidery than like pottery — you make a hole to make a stitch. </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/donate/\"><img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel2.jpg?resize=680%2C541&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"541\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel2.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel2.jpg?resize=320%2C255&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel2.jpg?resize=600%2C478&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel2.jpg?resize=240%2C191&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel2.jpg?resize=768%2C611&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p>So began a daily practice of collaborating with rather than forcing the clay, then embroidering the result — vessels to hold a life that says “YES” to itself, a life needful of constant reminding that all things forced are false and fragile. We need these reminders, all of us, if we are to be true to our own hearts. </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/donate/\"><img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel3.jpg?resize=680%2C459&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"459\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel3.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel3.jpg?resize=320%2C216&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel3.jpg?resize=600%2C405&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel3.jpg?resize=240%2C162&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel3.jpg?resize=768%2C518&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/donate/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel9.jpg?resize=680%2C592&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"592\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel9.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel9.jpg?resize=320%2C278&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel9.jpg?resize=600%2C522&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel9.jpg?resize=240%2C209&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel9.jpg?resize=768%2C668&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/donate/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel1.jpg?resize=680%2C688&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"688\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel1.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel1.jpg?resize=320%2C324&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel1.jpg?resize=600%2C607&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel1.jpg?resize=240%2C243&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel1.jpg?resize=768%2C777&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/donate/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel8.jpg?resize=680%2C597&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"597\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel8.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel8.jpg?resize=320%2C281&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel8.jpg?resize=600%2C527&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel8.jpg?resize=240%2C211&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel8.jpg?resize=768%2C674&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/donate/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel15.jpg?resize=680%2C598&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"598\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel15.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel15.jpg?resize=320%2C282&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel15.jpg?resize=600%2C528&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel15.jpg?resize=240%2C211&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel15.jpg?resize=768%2C676&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/donate/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel14.jpg?resize=680%2C657&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"657\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel14.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel14.jpg?resize=320%2C309&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel14.jpg?resize=600%2C580&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel14.jpg?resize=240%2C232&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel14.jpg?resize=768%2C742&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/donate/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel12.jpg?resize=680%2C573&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"573\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel12.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel12.jpg?resize=320%2C270&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel12.jpg?resize=600%2C506&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel12.jpg?resize=240%2C202&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel12.jpg?resize=768%2C648&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/donate/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel4.jpg?resize=680%2C706&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"706\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel4.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel4.jpg?resize=320%2C332&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel4.jpg?resize=600%2C623&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel4.jpg?resize=240%2C249&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel4.jpg?resize=768%2C797&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/donate/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel6.jpg?resize=680%2C722&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"722\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel6.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel6.jpg?resize=320%2C340&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel6.jpg?resize=600%2C637&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel6.jpg?resize=240%2C255&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel6.jpg?resize=768%2C815&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/donate/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessels_all.jpg?resize=680%2C620&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"620\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessels_all.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessels_all.jpg?resize=320%2C292&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessels_all.jpg?resize=600%2C547&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessels_all.jpg?resize=240%2C219&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessels_all.jpg?resize=768%2C700&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p>And so, as with my <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/tag/ceramics/\">other ceramics</a>, I am letting the impartial hand of chance, which forces nothing yet shapes everything, give a dozen of these vessels — yessels? — away: To enter the raffle, <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/donate/\">make a donation</a> by November 30 in any amount that feels unforced for you, so long as you end it with the decimal .12, whether it is $1.12 or $1,000.12. (For greater odds, consider joining my <a href=\"https://themarginalian.org/live\">twentieth anniversary celebration</a> — another set will be raffled off at the Museum of Delight there.)</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/donate/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel5.jpg?resize=680%2C545&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"545\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel5.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel5.jpg?resize=320%2C256&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel5.jpg?resize=600%2C481&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel5.jpg?resize=240%2C192&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/yessel5.jpg?resize=768%2C615&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p>And because the hand and the mind, the body and the spirit, are in constant conversation, somewhere along the way of this reckoning with life in clay and thread, a poem wrote itself in me:</p>\n<blockquote><p><strong>VESPER FOR A BURNING WORLD</strong><br />\n<em>by Maria Popova</em></p>\n<p>You need not be a saint,<br />\nstripped bare of all desire,<br />\nor a savior,<br />\ndragging the drowning<br />\nout of their pain<br />\nby the regret-stained collar<br />\nof their discontent.<br />\nYou need not leaven<br />\nthe world’s heavy toll of hope<br />\nby propping the sky up<br />\nwith your sunburnt hands<br />\nor fence yourself off<br />\nin the flowerless meadow<br />\nof detachment.<br />\nAll you need to do<br />\nis look in the mirror of morning<br />\nand say “Yes.”</p></blockquote>\n<hr /><h3>donating = loving</h3><p>For seventeen years, I have been spending hundreds of hours and thousands of dollars each month composing <em>The Marginalian</em> (which <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2021/10/22/brain-pickings-becoming-the-marginalian/\">bore the outgrown name <em>Brain Pickings</em></a> for its first fifteen years). It has remained free and ad-free and alive thanks to patronage from readers. I have no staff, no interns, no assistant — a thoroughly one-woman labor of love that is also my life and my livelihood. If this labor makes your own life more livable in any way, please consider lending a helping hand with a <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/donate/\">donation</a>. Your support makes all the difference.</p>\n\n<hr />\n\n<h3>newsletter</h3>\n<p><em>The Marginalian</em> has a free weekly newsletter. It comes out on Sundays and offers the week’s most inspiring reading. Here’s <a href=\"https://mailchi.mp/brainpickings/janna-levin-rebecca-elson-anne-lamott-james-gleick\">what to expect</a>. Like? <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/newsletter/\">Sign up.</a></p>","author":"Maria Popova","siteTitle":"The Marginalian","siteHash":"052ac1be0de11784b9ef27664fbcf33da8263d0e7cb9c6e601ccd959f2d3aa78","entryHash":"088e88271765432d539dbb438e055d35d19491c193fe3a3cde3264fdafce6d80","category":"Sites"}